WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.770
Sam finds a note on the kitchen table.

2
00:00:02.820 --> 00:00:05.050
It says: Es su casa.

3
00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:06.110
Simple enough.

4
00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:08.670
But Sam needs it in English.

5
00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:10.110
Is it his house?

6
00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:11.170
Her house?

7
00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:12.190
Their house?

8
00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:13.330
Your house?

9
00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:16.530
One little word, and
four possible owners.

10
00:00:16.580 --> 00:00:19.450
So how can Sam tell whose house it is?

11
00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:23.550
In this mission, you'll meet
the Spanish words for my, your,

12
00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:26.070
his, her, our and their,

13
00:00:26.120 --> 00:00:29.646
and watch "my" change when
there's more than one thing:

14
00:00:29.696 --> 00:00:31.710
mi casa, mis libros.

15
00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:36.750
Then you'll point at things with
this, that, these and those,

16
00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:39.390
and make each one agree with its noun.

17
00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:44.660
Your mission: work out who owns
what when Spanish says su.
